    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0119" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">855.24/9–1945</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of
                        the Office of Financial and Development Policy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Collado</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-09-19">September 19, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Crowley, Walter Thayer<anchor n="38" xml:id="d85-f1"/> and I had a meeting
                    this afternoon with Secretary Patterson<anchor n="39" xml:id="d85-f2"/> and
                    General Somervell,<anchor n="40" xml:id="d85-f3"/> and the following decisions
                    were made: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Reverse lend-lease ceases on the same day that lend-lease ceases.
                            However, for any services such as rent, transportation, etc., furnished
                            us by lend-lease countries after September 2, payment should be made by
                            giving them credit on their 3(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                            obligations or in surplus property.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>We are to tell Belgium that we recognize the obligation to balance the
                            lend-lease account with them and will do so in some way, probably by
                            delivery of surplus property.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. L. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
